cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jaxgam: JAX-accelerated Generalized Additive Models"
message: >-
  If you use jaxgam, please cite the underlying mgcv methodology.
  jaxgam is a Python port of Simon Wood's mgcv R package; the
  statistical methods are entirely his work.
type: software
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/scatt67/jaxgam"
authors:
  - family-names: Catts
    given-names: Shane

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Fast stable restricted maximum likelihood and marginal likelihood
      estimation of semiparametric generalized linear models
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
    journal: "Journal of the Royal Statistical Society (B)"
    volume: 73
    issue: 1
    start: 3
    end: 36
    year: 2011
    doi: "10.1111/j.1467-9868.2010.00749.x"
    scope: >-
      Core method for REML/ML estimation of GAMs. This is the primary
      reference for jaxgam's fitting algorithm (PIRLS + Laplace-approximate
      REML).

  - type: article
    title: >-
      Smoothing parameter and model selection for general smooth models
      (with discussion)
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
      - family-names: Pya
        given-names: N.
      - family-names: Säfken
        given-names: Benjamin
    journal: "Journal of the American Statistical Association"
    volume: 111
    start: 1548
    end: 1575
    year: 2016
    doi: "10.1080/01621459.2016.1180986"
    scope: >-
      Beyond exponential family models and general smooth model selection.

  - type: article
    title: "Generalized additive models for large datasets"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
      - family-names: Goude
        given-names: Y.
      - family-names: Shaw
        given-names: S.
    journal: "Journal of the Royal Statistical Society (C)"
    volume: 64
    issue: 1
    start: 139
    end: 155
    year: 2015
    doi: "10.1111/rssc.12068"
    scope: >-
      Large-dataset GAM fitting (bam), the basis of jaxgam's discretized
      route.

  - type: article
    title: >-
      Generalized additive models for gigadata: modelling the UK black
      smoke network daily data
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Z.
      - family-names: Shaddick
        given-names: G.
      - family-names: Augustin
        given-names: "N. H."
    journal: "Journal of the American Statistical Association"
    volume: 112
    issue: 519
    start: 1199
    end: 1210
    year: 2017
    doi: "10.1080/01621459.2016.1195744"
    scope: >-
      Covariate discretization and the performance iteration used by
      bam(discrete=TRUE) and by jaxgam's discretized route.

  - type: article
    title: >-
      Faster model matrix crossproducts for large generalized linear
      models with discretized covariates
    authors:
      - family-names: Li
        given-names: Z.
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
    journal: "Statistics and Computing"
    volume: 30
    start: 19
    end: 25
    year: 2020
    doi: "10.1007/s11222-019-09864-2"
    scope: >-
      Crossproduct algorithms for discretized covariates.

  - type: article
    title: >-
      A generalized Fellner-Schall method for smoothing parameter
      optimization with application to Tweedie location, scale and shape
      models
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
      - family-names: Fasiolo
        given-names: M.
    journal: "Biometrics"
    volume: 73
    issue: 4
    start: 1071
    end: 1081
    year: 2017
    doi: "10.1111/biom.12666"
    scope: >-
      The extended Fellner-Schall optimizer (optimizer="efs").

  - type: article
    title: >-
      Stable and efficient multiple smoothing parameter estimation for
      generalized additive models
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
    journal: "Journal of the American Statistical Association"
    volume: 99
    issue: 467
    start: 673
    end: 686
    year: 2004
    doi: "10.1198/016214504000000980"
    scope: >-
      GCV-based smoothing parameter estimation and the basics of GAMM.

  - type: book
    title: "Generalized Additive Models: An Introduction with R"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
    edition: "2"
    publisher:
      name: "Chapman and Hall/CRC"
    year: 2017
    scope: >-
      Comprehensive overview of GAM theory and mgcv implementation.

  - type: article
    title: "Thin-plate regression splines"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wood
        given-names: "Simon N."
    journal: "Journal of the Royal Statistical Society (B)"
    volume: 65
    issue: 1
    start: 95
    end: 114
    year: 2003
    doi: "10.1111/1467-9868.00374"
    scope: >-
      Thin plate regression splines, the default basis type in mgcv and
      jaxgam.
